# A mandatory copy like every other file under dev/env/ (see "Setting
# Up" in the README) - Podman Quadlet's EnvironmentFile= has no real
# "optional if missing" semantics (the leading "-" is only honored by
# systemd's own units, not by Quadlet's translation of a .container
# file into `podman run --env-file`; a missing file kept the container
# from starting at all with a raw "no such file or directory" instead
# of coming up cleanly without AWS wiring). The placeholder values
# below are enough for vb-api/vb-api-worker to start normally - only
# an actual downsync then fails with a clear error until real
# credentials are filled in.

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=change-me
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=change-me
AWS_BUCKET=vindobona2-at
AWS_REGION=eu-central-1
